- dblock has the most commits: 52 (18.2% of all commits). But they hold 565 non-blank lines (10.4%), or 725 counting blank lines (10.8%), which is third place.
- Vladimir Kochnev holds the most lines: 1,010 (18.7%), or 1,180 counting blank lines (17.6%). That comes from only 11 commits (3.8%).
- peter scholz is second on commits (34, 11.9%) but fifth on lines: 427 (7.9%), or 586 counting blank lines (8.7%).
- Many of peter scholz's commits were merges or committer-only actions. For example, he committed Brian van de Boogaard's 276 lines in "Add expose_nil option (#293)", and those lines are credited to Brian.

**Caveats**
- Surviving lines measure what is left in the code. They don't measure review skill, design knowledge, or deleted code.
- All figures above are printed by surviving-lines. The delegator totals come from the command `surviving-lines -- lib/grape_entity/delegator.rb lib/grape_entity/delegators lib/grape_entity/exposure/delegator_exposure.rb`. That grouping of files is my own choice of what counts as "the delegator code". I made no `.mailmap` changes.

